{
 "name": "Neighborhood Clinic",
 "idea": "",
 "brief": "One shared system for a small internal-medicine clinic. Collections: patients, bookings, reception, interviews, exams, prescriptions, stock, bills, notice (single item), summary (single item); value clock (starts 9:00).\nIntent rules:\n- Check in (inputs patient name, symptom): add reception entry with next number, clock time, status waiting, minutes waited 0. Judge urgency from symptom, patient's chronic conditions and age (chest tightness/pain, breathing trouble, fainting = high; fever, pain in older/chronic patients = medium; mild cold, refill = low). Mark that patient's booked booking arrived. Estimate wait from waiting people and urgency; rewrite notice (number called, expected wait, one line of guidance). Unknown names: add a new patient minimally.\n- Arrived: mark booking arrived and check in the same way using the booking purpose as symptom. Cancel: mark cancelled.\n- Send interview (reception number, description): add interview with summary, points to watch, note for doctor; set entry status interviewed; raise/lower urgency if warranted.\n- Call in (chosen entry): set it to with doctor; anyone already with doctor becomes to pay; update notice and the \"with doctor\" value.\n- Record exam (doctor's note): add exam record for the entry with assessment, draft prescription, next visit, using note and interview.\n- Prescribe (exam record): create prescription rows (medicine, dose, days), check allergies, conditions, interactions, write warning (or \"none\"); reduce stock by plausible amounts; if left < minimum set on order.\n- To billing: set entry to to pay if not; add bill with estimated amount (consultation about 1,500 yen-style or $ amounts, use USD) and breakdown from exam and prescriptions, paid false.\n- Paid: bill paid, entry done, rewrite summary (check-ins, seen, average wait, attention point in one sentence).\n- Next 10 minutes: clock +10, every non-done entry minutes waited +10, sometimes add a believable walk-in, rewrite notice and summary.\n- Order: set stock on order (add reorder quantity) for the medicine.\nAlways keep the notice and summary current.",
